            "review_title": "Review at An Viet Thon Restaurant",
            "review_text": "V00Doo\nKuala Lumpur, Malaysia529 contributions\n0\nRecommended by our hotel for authentic Vietnamese cuisine\nJan 2020\nQuite a large open-air restaurant (but with large mobile overhead rain cover if needed). Popular with locals. HUGE menu with regular meats but also unusual game meat. For 4 adults, we ordered a springroll starter, lotus stem salad (Gỏi Ngó Sen - best choice ever!), a seafood noodle, grilled beef with passionfruit sauce (tasted weird), stirfried ladies fingers or okra and simple vietnamese tea.\nLots of colourful hanging lights and lanterns - a little OTT but I guess it's because of Tet (Lunar New Year) celebrations\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 28, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
